WEBVTT

00:01.127 --> 00:04.815
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.830 --> 00:08.098
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:08.133 --> 00:11.668
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.703 --> 00:14.671
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.706 --> 00:18.174
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.210 --> 00:21.511
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.546 --> 00:23.113
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.148 --> 00:24.514
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.549 --> 00:30.019
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.528 --> 00:38.043
You guys know what this meeting's about?

00:38.044 --> 00:40.530
- No idea.
- How about you, Morning Breath Mike?

00:40.565 --> 00:43.066
I have no idea.

00:43.101 --> 00:44.267
Listen up, everyone.

00:44.302 --> 00:45.902
Sales are down across the board,

00:45.937 --> 00:47.537
but mostly we're failing to connect

00:47.572 --> 00:49.906
with a group called "millennials."

00:49.941 --> 00:52.175
I saw this guy cry one time.

00:52.210 --> 00:54.177
To learn more
about our target demographic,

00:54.212 --> 00:56.813
we're all gonna watch
this instructional video.

00:58.022 --> 00:59.164
<i>News on the March</i>

00:59.165 --> 01:01.988
<i>Millennials. Who are they?
What do the want?</i>

01:01.989 --> 01:03.386
<i>A millennial can be defined</i>

01:03.421 --> 01:07.190
<i>as anyone born between 1982 and 2000.</i>

01:07.225 --> 01:10.560
<i>Or anyone who thinks loving
sriracha or Austin, Texas,</i>

01:10.595 --> 01:12.695
<i>counts as a personality.</i>

01:12.731 --> 01:14.497
<i>Millennials crave things like:</i>

01:14.533 --> 01:15.765
<i>instant gratification,</i>

01:15.800 --> 01:17.433
<i>authentic experiences,</i>

01:17.469 --> 01:19.702
<i>and, for some reason
we haven't figured out yet,</i>

01:19.738 --> 01:21.538
<i>improv comedy.</i>

01:21.573 --> 01:23.740
<i>Here's one millennial who has a parakeet</i>

01:23.775 --> 01:26.743
<i>with nine million followers on Snapchat.</i>

01:26.778 --> 01:28.745
<i>Here's another
who singlehandedly started</i>

01:28.780 --> 01:31.781
<i>the hashtags that cancelled
12 network TV shows</i>

01:31.816 --> 01:33.616
<i>she found offensive.</i>

01:33.652 --> 01:36.119
<i>And now I'm told
she identifies as a man,</i>

01:36.154 --> 01:38.121
<i>so I'm being fired.</i>

01:38.156 --> 01:40.557
<i>Hello. I'm your new announcer.</i>

01:40.592 --> 01:42.292
<i>And actually, he was just about done.</i>

01:42.327 --> 01:45.128
<i>Thank you and good day.</i>

01:45.163 --> 01:48.164
So please welcome someone who's
gonna help us reach millennials,

01:48.200 --> 01:50.600
our new head of social media, Hammer.

01:52.704 --> 01:54.671
Oh. He just group-texted us "hello."

01:54.706 --> 01:56.506
And now here comes a text

01:56.541 --> 01:58.908
from the guy who doesn't know
this is a group text.

01:58.944 --> 02:01.344
"Nice to meet you, Hammer.
Let's have lunch later,

02:01.379 --> 02:03.146
and I'll tell you who's gay."

02:03.181 --> 02:04.814
Right on. 'Sup? I'm Hammer.

02:04.849 --> 02:07.450
<i>Uh, first I'd like
to not thank you for hiring me,</i>

02:07.485 --> 02:09.852
because I just expect
good things to happen to me

02:09.888 --> 02:11.354
without working for them.

02:11.389 --> 02:14.624
Second, I'd like to give you all
a list of my trigger warnings.

02:14.659 --> 02:16.125
What's a trigger warning?

02:16.161 --> 02:18.394
Actually, brah, asking me
what a trigger warning is

02:18.430 --> 02:19.896
is one of my triggers, brah.

02:19.931 --> 02:21.197
I feel traumatized, brah.

02:21.233 --> 02:23.032
And now I'm tweeting about you, brah.

02:23.068 --> 02:24.367
And now you're trending, brah.

02:24.402 --> 02:26.169
And now your life is ruined, brah.

02:26.204 --> 02:27.837
And now you're fired, brah.

02:28.873 --> 02:30.807
What... what happened to Brah?

02:30.842 --> 02:33.676
Also, the lack of diversity here
is horrifying, brah.

02:33.712 --> 02:35.445
Uh, Brah is gone.

02:35.480 --> 02:37.714
Now, if we want to get
some social media attention,

02:37.749 --> 02:39.682
we got to start with a group selfie.

02:39.718 --> 02:42.986
Um, excuse me. Didn't Ellen
do this, like, three years ago?

02:43.021 --> 02:45.788
<i>Hey, does Taye Diggs
follow you on Twitter?</i>

02:45.824 --> 02:48.091
No, but Kraft Singles does.

02:48.126 --> 02:50.526
That's what I thought.

02:51.596 --> 02:52.929
And... posted.

02:52.964 --> 02:55.798
Do you know what I just did?
I just made you all viral.

02:55.834 --> 02:58.801
Also, my band is playing tonight
at an inconvenient time.

02:58.837 --> 03:01.704
It's six un-showered guys
and a pale woman with a ukulele

03:01.740 --> 03:03.539
shouting "Hey!" in unison.

03:03.575 --> 03:06.009
Because that's what music is now.

03:08.113 --> 03:09.178
♪ Hey! ♪

03:11.216 --> 03:12.382
♪ Hey! ♪

03:12.417 --> 03:14.751
What is this?
They just keep saying "hey."

03:14.786 --> 03:17.654
I know. It's my favorite song.

03:20.358 --> 03:23.326
Oh, 'cause "hay" is for horses.

03:27.365 --> 03:29.465
Hey, guys.
You want to have a smoke break?

03:29.501 --> 03:31.501
What? We can't smoke inside.

03:31.536 --> 03:33.536
It's not smoking, Peter. It's vaping.

03:33.571 --> 03:35.805
Everyone's doing it... Even Darth Vaper.

03:37.909 --> 03:40.743
I find your lack of vape disturbing.

03:40.779 --> 03:42.779
Come on, Peter, give it a shot.

03:53.758 --> 03:55.458
What happened? All of a sudden

03:55.493 --> 03:57.860
I feel like I know better
than everyone else!

03:57.896 --> 04:00.129
That's because anytime
someone walks through a cloud

04:00.165 --> 04:02.498
of vape smoke, a millennial is born.

04:02.534 --> 04:03.933
I think I feel it!

04:03.968 --> 04:06.002
<i>Broad City is so funny.</i>

04:06.037 --> 04:08.204
<i>No, Broad City is genius.</i>

04:08.239 --> 04:11.140
<i>No, no. Broad City is everything!</i>

04:11.176 --> 04:13.376
There it is. Grossly exaggerating

04:13.411 --> 04:16.079
the quality of a just-okay TV show.

04:16.114 --> 04:19.015
Peter, you're officially a millennial.

04:19.050 --> 04:21.517
<i>Hey, you want a ride
in the Millennial Falcon?</i>

04:21.553 --> 04:24.253
Ah, look at that...
We found another one!

04:27.926 --> 04:30.126
Peter, a rite of passage
for any millennial

04:30.161 --> 04:32.028
is attending Coachella.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.496
It's a great place to see bands

04:33.531 --> 04:35.331
that are either really new
or really old.

04:35.367 --> 04:37.600
- Which one should we see?
- Well, on the main stage,

04:37.635 --> 04:40.770
it's Tame Impala that formed
in an UberPOOL on the way here.

04:40.805 --> 04:43.039
And on the side stage,
it's "Neil Young asleep"

04:43.074 --> 04:44.640
in front of the television."

04:47.779 --> 04:51.114
<i>I always get him confused with
Bloom County's Bill the Cat.</i>

04:56.654 --> 04:58.554
Peter, you're doing great
as a millennial.

04:58.590 --> 05:01.290
Next thing is you got to learn
how to be on Fleek.

05:01.326 --> 05:04.927
"On fleek"? People still say "on fleek"?

05:04.963 --> 05:06.529
No, Peter, that's not what I meant.

05:06.564 --> 05:08.131
I want you on Fleek.

05:08.166 --> 05:09.465
This is Fleek.

05:09.501 --> 05:11.000
Oh, can I ride him?!

05:11.035 --> 05:13.035
Sure, Peter. Get on Fleek.

05:13.071 --> 05:15.605
♪ ♪

05:16.641 --> 05:18.141
Yay!

05:19.344 --> 05:20.977
♪ ♪

05:24.549 --> 05:27.016
Our country's involved
in six different wars,

05:27.051 --> 05:29.852
<i>but millennials think about this stuff.</i>

05:33.458 --> 05:35.425
Remember, Peter, never walk anywhere

05:35.460 --> 05:37.660
when you can ride
something weird instead.

05:37.695 --> 05:39.796
What's that?
Sorry, I was taking a selfie

05:39.831 --> 05:42.398
while shooting a Snapchat
while Periscoping that Snapchat

05:42.434 --> 05:45.001
while Instagramming latte art
while Shazaming The Weekend

05:45.036 --> 05:48.271
<i>while streaming Master of None
while retweeting George Takei</i>

05:48.306 --> 05:50.106
while saying, "This wins the Internet!"

05:50.141 --> 05:53.576
while still being ♪soooo bored.

05:53.611 --> 05:55.311
Hammer?

05:55.346 --> 05:58.414
Hammer? Come on, man, don't
make me look up from my phone.

05:58.450 --> 06:00.450
Oh, you're texting me.

06:14.799 --> 06:16.866
Oh, no! Hammer!

06:18.169 --> 06:19.469
You! Call 911!

06:19.504 --> 06:21.337
You! Give me your shirt
to make a tourniquet!

06:21.372 --> 06:23.706
You! Snap a pic.
Clarendon filter. Clarendon!

06:23.741 --> 06:25.475
Hammer, stay with me, buddy.

06:25.510 --> 06:27.477
Peter, if I die,

06:27.512 --> 06:32.148
chop my body up
and serve me as street tacos.

06:34.619 --> 06:36.185
So selfless.

06:36.221 --> 06:39.856
No! I won't let you be made into tacos!

06:39.891 --> 06:42.358
Peter... it's-it's too late.

06:42.393 --> 06:45.828
Listen, I've got this idea
for a business, and...

06:45.864 --> 06:47.830
I want you to have it.

06:47.866 --> 06:49.665
It's artisanal.

06:49.701 --> 06:51.868
A-Artisanal...

06:53.338 --> 06:55.238
Artisanal what? Is it pretzels?

06:55.273 --> 06:56.906
Is it artisanal pretzels?!

06:56.941 --> 06:58.307
Has that been done?

06:58.343 --> 07:01.477
Does anyone know if
artisanal pretzels is a thing?

07:01.513 --> 07:05.047
It seems so obvious, yet I
don't think I've ever seen them.

07:05.083 --> 07:06.949
I better do millennial CPR.

07:06.985 --> 07:08.284
One... ugh, whatever...

07:08.319 --> 07:09.785
Two... ugh, whatever...

07:09.821 --> 07:12.522
Three... ugh, I'm gonna let
my parents take care of this.

07:21.071 --> 07:23.238
I've never been to a millennial funeral.

07:23.274 --> 07:26.675
Yeah, it seems in poor taste
that they hired Keyboard Cat.

07:31.849 --> 07:34.049
Assembled congregants,

07:34.084 --> 07:36.151
no worries to you.

07:36.187 --> 07:37.953
And also to you.

07:37.988 --> 07:40.155
Let us tweet.

07:41.458 --> 07:43.258
Peter, why is he naked in there?

07:43.294 --> 07:45.260
It's an environmental statement.

07:45.296 --> 07:48.130
Lois, please stop looking
at my dead friend's dong.

07:48.165 --> 07:50.299
<i>Listen, I made breakfast and drove,</i>

07:50.334 --> 07:53.335
so if there's a dead dong,
I'm gonna look at it!

07:54.939 --> 07:58.273
We've all lost
a great friend-slash-barista-

07:58.309 --> 08:00.142
slash-deejay-

08:00.177 --> 08:02.511
slash-Genius Bar employee-

08:02.546 --> 08:04.846
slash-person with a yellow highlighter

08:04.882 --> 08:06.715
at the Best Buy exit.

08:06.750 --> 08:10.152
And now a reading
from the book of JustJared.

08:10.187 --> 08:13.522
"Death be the ultimate fail."

08:13.557 --> 08:15.424
Peter, I hate to do this here,

08:15.459 --> 08:17.259
but you were good friends with Hammer,

08:17.294 --> 08:19.394
and business at the brewery must go on.

08:19.430 --> 08:20.996
That's why, as of today,

08:21.031 --> 08:23.098
I'm making you head of social media.

08:23.133 --> 08:25.300
Hey, whatever you want.
I'm a team player.

08:25.336 --> 08:27.603
<i>I was even one of the 300.</i>

08:28.839 --> 08:30.839
Hey, does 299 work?

08:30.874 --> 08:33.675
'Cause I got to go diarrhea
off the cliff.

08:37.481 --> 08:41.016
<i>We now return to Marvel's The Offenders.</i>

08:41.051 --> 08:43.285
Good morning, you see.

08:43.320 --> 08:45.587
I gathered you all together...
Kevin Spacey,

08:45.623 --> 08:47.022
Roman Polanski...

08:47.057 --> 08:48.523
Hey, hey, hey...

08:48.559 --> 08:50.659
Woody Allen, Steven Seagal,

08:50.694 --> 08:53.395
Matt Lauer with the Pudding Pop,

08:53.430 --> 08:54.630
Brett Ratner,

08:54.665 --> 08:58.600
and you, lesser-known offender
James Toback.

08:58.636 --> 09:00.235
Don't forget me!

09:01.405 --> 09:03.038
Harvey shower!

09:03.073 --> 09:05.407
I-I... I-Is Matt Damon coming?

09:05.442 --> 09:07.676
No, but he knows about all of us.

09:07.711 --> 09:11.947
He's very aware of what's
going on here, you see.

09:11.982 --> 09:14.483
All right, guys, I got to come
up with some social media ideas

09:14.518 --> 09:15.851
for the brewery. What do ya got?

09:15.886 --> 09:17.919
Oh, you want viral?
You asked the right guy.

09:17.955 --> 09:19.955
You remember Leeroy Jenkins?

09:19.990 --> 09:21.623
- Yeah.
- Right.

09:21.659 --> 09:24.126
- What do you mean, "right"?
- You know, Leeroy Jenkins.

09:24.161 --> 09:25.794
- What about him?
- Do that.

09:25.829 --> 09:27.896
Joe, you can't... That already happened.

09:27.931 --> 09:29.965
Do it again. This time with beer.

09:30.000 --> 09:31.633
Hang on a sec.

09:39.677 --> 09:42.311
- Thank you.
- How about some fruit in the beer?

09:42.346 --> 09:44.680
No, guys, we need
social media-specific plans

09:44.715 --> 09:46.148
to reach a younger audience.

09:46.183 --> 09:48.317
You remember "Charlie Bit My Finger"?

09:49.320 --> 09:50.585
Do that.

09:50.621 --> 09:52.587
You know what? I give up.
We've given this...

09:52.623 --> 09:53.855
what, almost a minute?

09:53.891 --> 09:55.557
Peter, that's the problem
with kids today...

09:55.592 --> 09:57.059
They have no attention span.

09:57.094 --> 09:58.627
Wait. That's it!

09:58.662 --> 10:01.196
We'll do a show for people
with no attention span.

10:01.231 --> 10:04.166
<i>We'll call it The Six Second Talk Show.</i>

10:04.201 --> 10:06.501
Well, I guess that could work.
But it's just so sad

10:06.537 --> 10:07.836
that young people can't pay attention

10:07.871 --> 10:09.271
to something longer than six sec...

10:11.041 --> 10:13.642
Oh, oh, my God.

10:13.677 --> 10:14.910
JOE and PETER and CLEVELAND: Whoa!

10:14.945 --> 10:16.611
What the hell, you guys? I was talking.

10:16.647 --> 10:19.081
You know, there's more to life
than just what's on your phone.

10:19.116 --> 10:20.315
Wrong, idiot.

10:23.787 --> 10:26.288
Anyone know how
to turn these things off?

10:30.527 --> 10:32.094
<i>All right, Six Second Talk Show</i>

10:32.129 --> 10:34.229
in three, two...

10:34.264 --> 10:36.531
<i>I'm Peter Griffin, and this is
the Six Second Talk Show.</i>

10:36.567 --> 10:38.066
My guest tonight is Joe Biden.

10:38.102 --> 10:40.569
And that's all the time we have.
Thanks for watching. Good night.

10:40.604 --> 10:42.437
- How was that?
- Eh, it kind of dragged.

10:43.374 --> 10:45.006
Well, Congress is at it again.

10:45.042 --> 10:46.108
Good night.

10:48.512 --> 10:50.212
<i>It's The Six Second Talk Show,</i>

10:50.247 --> 10:54.316
and now, your host, here...

10:56.854 --> 10:58.587
<i>Welcome to The Six Second Talk Show.</i>

10:58.622 --> 11:01.823
I'm Peter Griffin, and now our
musical guest, Barenaked Ladies.

11:01.859 --> 11:03.558
- ♪ It's been... ♪
- I'd like to thank our musical guest,

11:03.594 --> 11:04.826
Barenaked Ladies. Good night.

11:08.132 --> 11:09.598
Peter, I can't believe your talk show

11:09.633 --> 11:11.800
is such a huge hit for the brewery.

11:11.835 --> 11:15.170
And thanks to that, I'm now
a huge social media star.

11:17.708 --> 11:19.674
Oh, my God, what the hell is that?

11:19.710 --> 11:20.976
Hello, Griffin family.

11:21.011 --> 11:23.445
I'm coming to you live,
via living room hologram.

11:23.480 --> 11:26.047
I'm Parker Stanton, CEO of Boop,

11:26.083 --> 11:28.717
the most powerful company
in Silicon Valley.

11:28.752 --> 11:30.218
- Do you know Mr. Skin?
- Do you know Mr. Skin?

11:30.254 --> 11:31.586
- Ah!
- Ah!

11:31.622 --> 11:32.954
- We'll talk later.
- We'll talk later.

11:32.990 --> 11:34.689
Look, Peter, the reason I'm here

11:34.725 --> 11:36.625
<i>is because of your Six Second Talk Show.</i>

11:36.660 --> 11:38.226
Now, I haven't had the time to watch it,

11:38.262 --> 11:40.362
but I hear it's the buzz
of Silicon Valley.

11:40.397 --> 11:42.998
I want you and your family
to visit us here as my guests,

11:43.033 --> 11:45.267
so I can find out
what the next big thing is.

11:45.302 --> 11:46.802
Oh, I-I got lots of ideas.

11:46.837 --> 11:50.071
I've been working on something
called "Look At It, Kick It."

11:52.443 --> 11:53.975
Look at it...

11:54.011 --> 11:55.744
Excuse me, can I help you?

11:55.779 --> 11:57.345
Kick it!

11:57.381 --> 11:58.847
Pure genius.

11:58.882 --> 12:01.416
See you in Silicon Valley.

12:01.452 --> 12:02.818
Oh, this is exciting.

12:02.853 --> 12:04.119
A family trip.

12:04.154 --> 12:05.587
Yeah, I love traveling.

12:05.622 --> 12:07.856
Oh, except that trip to Europe
where we spent most of our time

12:07.891 --> 12:10.158
trying to refold our map.

12:10.194 --> 12:12.160
All right, the museum is that way,

12:12.196 --> 12:14.196
so let's fold the map and go.

12:18.268 --> 12:20.635
Okay, couple more folds...

12:20.671 --> 12:22.437
Nope, okay, wrong end.

12:22.473 --> 12:23.839
Now, let's see...

12:23.874 --> 12:25.340
Nope, nope, that's wrong...

12:25.375 --> 12:26.541
Find the corners.

12:26.577 --> 12:27.776
It's not a puzzle, Chris.

12:27.811 --> 12:29.478
Y-You got to fold on the creases.

12:29.513 --> 12:30.812
I'd be able to find the creases

12:30.848 --> 12:33.014
if somebody had folded it
correctly last time.

12:33.050 --> 12:34.516
I did fold it correctly.

12:34.551 --> 12:36.585
Nope, you didn't, and then,
you jammed it into a backpack

12:36.620 --> 12:37.919
and now I'm in this mess.

12:37.955 --> 12:39.554
Don't blame me, you ripped it up

12:39.590 --> 12:41.723
when you were tearing through
the backpack for your snacks.

12:41.758 --> 12:44.092
Okay, this is why I wanted
to bring a globe, all right?

12:44.127 --> 12:45.427
You don't have to fold a globe.

12:45.462 --> 12:48.330
Who the hell would bring
a globe on vacation?

12:48.365 --> 12:50.031
See, Bon? We're eating food,

12:50.067 --> 12:52.200
and they're tearing each other apart.

12:52.236 --> 12:55.203
<i>Where to next, mon ch├йri?</i>

13:00.377 --> 13:01.943
Welcome to Boop.

13:01.979 --> 13:04.713
As our name suggests,
our mainframe connects to

13:04.748 --> 13:07.716
and powers virtually
every server on the globe.

13:07.751 --> 13:10.819
Without Boop, there is no Internet.

13:10.854 --> 13:12.287
Hey, Parker. Are we still on

13:12.322 --> 13:14.689
for the Samsung Galaxy Note
meeting after lunch?

13:14.725 --> 13:16.157
Yep. Are-are the test results in?

13:16.193 --> 13:17.459
Yeah, but...

13:17.494 --> 13:19.794
Let's save it for the meeting.

13:19.830 --> 13:20.929
Where's your nearest bathroom?

13:20.964 --> 13:21.997
Gender-fluid?

13:22.032 --> 13:24.099
Yes, there will be a lot of that.

13:25.936 --> 13:29.504
Hmm, must be one of them
high-tech Japanese toilets.

13:30.741 --> 13:34.776
♪ I'm gonna pee into electrical urinal ♪

13:34.811 --> 13:37.045
♪ And make the sparks go higher. ♪

13:37.080 --> 13:39.180
I'm having so much fun.

13:41.785 --> 13:43.818
What the hell is going on?

13:43.854 --> 13:45.787
Our mainframe is having a meltdown!

13:45.822 --> 13:47.255
Hang on, let me flush.

13:48.992 --> 13:50.225
You idiot.

13:50.260 --> 13:52.027
You shut down the entire Internet.

13:52.062 --> 13:53.395
How could you do that?

13:53.430 --> 13:55.564
This is the most irresponsible
thing that I've ever...

13:55.599 --> 13:57.432
<i>Although I was incensed by this man,</i>

13:57.467 --> 14:00.735
<i>I had to admire his courage
for leaving his penis out</i>

14:00.771 --> 14:02.804
<i>the entire time I was yelling at him.</i>

14:02.839 --> 14:05.307
<i>As a man who struggles
with body dysmorphia,</i>

14:05.342 --> 14:06.875
<i>I couldn't help but be impressed</i>

14:06.910 --> 14:09.177
<i>by that kind of self-confidence.</i>

14:09.212 --> 14:11.980
<i>As I stood there,
being berated by this man,</i>

14:12.015 --> 14:15.083
<i>I couldn't help but notice
his searching gaze.</i>

14:15.118 --> 14:17.052
<i>Years later,
we would bump into each other</i>

14:17.087 --> 14:20.221
<i>at a small cafe in Rome and
reminisce about this moment.</i>

14:20.257 --> 14:23.558
<i>And later still, recreate it
in a small bed and breakfast</i>

14:23.594 --> 14:25.360
<i>at the bottom of the Spanish Steps.</i>

14:25.395 --> 14:27.729
<i>But that's a story for another time.</i>

14:27.764 --> 14:30.832
<i>Or, as they say in Italian, molto homo.</i>

14:38.705 --> 14:40.305
Peter, you've done some stupid things,

14:40.340 --> 14:42.774
but crashing the Internet has
to be the dumbest yet.

14:42.809 --> 14:45.744
Look at the chaos you've caused.

14:48.248 --> 14:50.949
I have no idea
how to drive without texting.

14:52.920 --> 14:54.986
Why can't I post this video?

14:55.022 --> 14:57.122
- Hello.
- What did you say?

14:57.157 --> 14:59.424
Why aren't you looking
at your phone, you psycho?

14:59.459 --> 15:01.092
Why is no one liking my posts?

15:01.128 --> 15:02.494
<i>Well, I hate all your posts!</i>

15:02.529 --> 15:03.628
Hello.

15:12.239 --> 15:14.472
Hello.

15:14.508 --> 15:15.574
Peter, Lois is right.

15:15.609 --> 15:16.841
This mess is all your fault.

15:16.877 --> 15:18.209
Settle down, Brian.

15:18.245 --> 15:20.378
I'm sure life will be just fine
without the Internet.

15:20.414 --> 15:23.281
Maybe we can even go see
that Amish comedian.

15:23.317 --> 15:24.783
Sir, where are you from?

15:24.818 --> 15:25.884
Chicago.

15:25.919 --> 15:27.586
I have never been to Chicago.

15:27.621 --> 15:28.820
How about you, sir?

15:28.855 --> 15:29.888
Boston!

15:29.923 --> 15:31.423
I have never been to Boston.

15:31.458 --> 15:34.960
Anyone here from the back fields
of Pennsylvania, Ohio

15:34.995 --> 15:36.127
or upstate New York?

15:36.163 --> 15:37.295
No!

15:37.331 --> 15:40.432
Then I have been Jebediah, son of Abner.

15:42.536 --> 15:44.402
How are we gonna get back
to the airport?

15:44.438 --> 15:46.404
There's no Internet,
which means there's no GPS,

15:46.440 --> 15:47.906
which means we can't use Uber.

15:47.941 --> 15:49.307
Okay, I have a crazy idea.

15:49.343 --> 15:50.475
Let's get a cab.

15:50.510 --> 15:52.177
There's a taxi stand.

15:53.213 --> 15:55.113
Dead.

15:55.148 --> 15:56.214
Dead...

15:56.249 --> 15:57.549
Dead.

15:57.584 --> 15:58.650
Barely alive.

15:58.685 --> 15:59.784
To the airport.

16:02.823 --> 16:04.889
Now, because you can't stare
at your phone anymore,

16:04.925 --> 16:08.793
enjoy a disturbingly loud clip
of Jimmy Fallon on cab TV.

16:08.829 --> 16:11.196
Tonight, get ready to lose
all respect for Al Pacino

16:11.231 --> 16:13.798
when I force him to play a game
meant for children!

16:13.834 --> 16:14.899
This.

16:14.935 --> 16:16.801
This is why Uber.

16:20.474 --> 16:24.242
No Netflix, no Hulu, no Amazon...

16:24.277 --> 16:25.877
I'm so bored.

16:25.912 --> 16:27.712
Come on, Meg, you're overreacting.

16:27.748 --> 16:29.447
We still got network TV.

16:29.483 --> 16:33.184
<i>We now return to Kevin Can Wait on CBS.</i>

16:33.220 --> 16:34.352
Well, that's not gonna work.

16:34.388 --> 16:35.887
Okay, everybody, don't panic.

16:35.922 --> 16:38.223
We'll just do what people did
before the Internet.

16:38.258 --> 16:39.391
We can play charades.

16:39.426 --> 16:41.192
Oh, you mean like your marriage?

16:41.228 --> 16:43.228
Chris, I told you that in confidence.

16:43.263 --> 16:44.629
Dad, you got to do something.

16:44.665 --> 16:46.464
Nobody can live without the Internet.

16:46.500 --> 16:48.233
Ah, you're right. This sucks.

16:48.268 --> 16:50.135
It's even worse
than when I was roommates

16:50.170 --> 16:51.569
with Oscar Pistorius.

16:51.605 --> 16:53.271
Somebody's in here.

16:53.306 --> 16:56.007
Somebody's in here!

16:56.043 --> 16:57.609
I'm the one who screwed this up.

16:57.644 --> 16:59.310
I'll be the one to fix it.

16:59.346 --> 17:01.112
I'll be the Internet.

17:01.148 --> 17:02.547
What are you talking about?

17:02.582 --> 17:04.849
We can do all the things
we loved about the Internet.

17:04.885 --> 17:06.751
We just got to do it without technology.

17:06.787 --> 17:08.787
From now on,
if you want to tweet something,

17:08.822 --> 17:10.255
you do it the old-fashioned way:

17:10.290 --> 17:11.656
write it on a piece of paper,

17:11.692 --> 17:14.492
staple it to a bird,
and throw it out the door.

17:18.699 --> 17:20.899
Hey, do you follow Peter Griffin
on Twitter?

17:20.934 --> 17:22.534
No. Why? Is he funny?

17:22.569 --> 17:24.469
No, he just throws dead birds
on his lawn.

17:24.504 --> 17:25.870
It's awesome.

17:29.743 --> 17:31.576
Great news, Chris. I figured out

17:31.611 --> 17:33.678
how to recreate the best part of
the Internet.

17:33.714 --> 17:35.714
I've got pictures of five celebrities

17:35.749 --> 17:37.615
who you'd never believe used to be fat.

17:37.651 --> 17:39.984
- Great, let's see 'em.
- Sure, buddy.

17:40.020 --> 17:43.521
But first you have to watch
this unwelcome pop-up ad.

17:43.557 --> 17:45.690
I don't want probiotics.

17:45.726 --> 17:47.058
Then press the "skip ad" button.

17:47.094 --> 17:48.993
Why should I do all this work?

17:49.029 --> 17:50.829
They're really good pictures, Chris.

17:50.864 --> 17:52.564
Number three will shock you.

17:52.599 --> 17:54.199
Okay, I'll press it.

17:54.234 --> 17:56.267
Oh, no! You pressed in the wrong place,

17:56.303 --> 17:58.403
and now you're being sent
to the ad's website,

17:58.438 --> 18:00.271
which also has additional pop-ups.

18:00.307 --> 18:01.673
This is a nightmare!

18:01.708 --> 18:03.174
Just tell me one of 'em.

18:03.210 --> 18:04.375
Kenan Thompson.

18:04.411 --> 18:06.644
That's not a surprise!

18:09.416 --> 18:10.815
Peter? What are you doing?

18:10.851 --> 18:12.751
Oh, I'm your Waze app today.

18:12.786 --> 18:14.419
- You on your way to work?
- Yeah, I am.

18:14.454 --> 18:16.588
All right, you will be there
in six minutes.

18:16.623 --> 18:17.822
Just start heading straight.

18:17.858 --> 18:19.224
Okay, sounds good.

18:21.261 --> 18:23.962
- So, how's everything at...
- Take a right! Right now!

18:25.098 --> 18:26.564
Geez, okay, calm down.

18:26.600 --> 18:28.166
Left! Take a left immediately!

18:32.973 --> 18:34.339
Would you like to upgrade

18:34.374 --> 18:36.908
to an ad-free experience for $4.99?

18:36.943 --> 18:40.245
- No.
- Try new Domino's Pizza.

18:44.785 --> 18:46.618
Hey, Peter, who are these guys?

18:46.653 --> 18:48.119
Oh, this is just my looping GIF

18:48.155 --> 18:51.356
of black teens reacting
to a very mild burn.

18:51.391 --> 18:53.091
Huh. Sounds kind of pointless.

18:53.126 --> 18:54.292
Oh, you mean like your feet?

19:05.138 --> 19:07.572
All right, trying to be
the Internet is impossible.

19:07.607 --> 19:09.641
I wish I never peed on that server.

19:09.676 --> 19:11.242
You know, when my phone gets wet,

19:11.278 --> 19:12.710
I just put it in a bag of rice.

19:12.746 --> 19:14.045
Shut up, Meg. That's dumb.

19:14.080 --> 19:15.680
I've done that before. It works.

19:15.715 --> 19:17.382
Chris, that's brilliant.

19:17.417 --> 19:19.584
We just need a big bag
and a lot of rice.

19:19.619 --> 19:21.019
You sure that's gonna work?

19:21.054 --> 19:22.220
Eh, worth a shot.

19:22.255 --> 19:23.688
We'll just have to roll up our sleeves

19:23.723 --> 19:25.089
and do the best we can,

19:25.125 --> 19:27.659
like the men who built New York City.

19:27.694 --> 19:31.229
Men, creating an entire
subway system out of nothing

19:31.264 --> 19:34.299
is grueling, thankless,
life-threatening work.

19:34.334 --> 19:36.501
But just remember: we're doing this

19:36.536 --> 19:39.370
so that one day,
future commuters can be hassled

19:39.406 --> 19:42.473
by panhandlers
and amateur break-dancers.

19:42.509 --> 19:44.375
What about public masturbators?

19:44.411 --> 19:46.611
Especially public masturbators.

19:46.646 --> 19:49.113
Now, let's go die underground!

19:57.524 --> 19:59.791
Look, we're getting a signal.

19:59.826 --> 20:01.192
I think we fixed the Internet.

20:01.228 --> 20:02.393
Something's coming through.

20:02.429 --> 20:03.795
It looks like an ad.

20:03.830 --> 20:06.698
"Smithwick's Artisinal Pretzels."

20:06.733 --> 20:09.100
Son of a bitch!

20:14.474 --> 20:16.841
Well, I'm glad you got the Internet...

20:16.877 --> 20:19.110
H-Hold on.

20:19.145 --> 20:21.012
I'm sorry, what-what were you saying?

20:21.047 --> 20:22.580
Yeah, sounds good.

20:22.616 --> 20:25.149
And send.

20:25.185 --> 20:28.052
Take that, Delta Air Lines.

20:39.499 --> 20:41.065
Submitted for your approval:

20:41.101 --> 20:44.335
a restaurant full of people
so distracted by their phones,

20:44.371 --> 20:47.538
they're unaware that they're all
about to go up in smoke,

20:47.574 --> 20:50.041
just like the Fox Tuesday night lineup.

21:00.024 --> 21:03.024
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru